{
  "about": "Spike S9 (design doc 0095): model outputs that mean a refusal, plus controls, for the three scan engines. `kind`: refusal (signalled by the provider or the CLI; must end `refused`), unsignalled (a plain-text refusal with no provider signal; must never end `succeeded`), control (not a refusal; checks the mapping does not over-match), risk (a refusal no mapping can see; recorded as a known model risk, not counted in the bar). `source` says where the wording comes from. Live refusal rates need credits (S2/S3 are BLOCKED on Unified Billing), so none of these are live recordings of a refusal.",
  "fixtures": [
    {
      "id": "B1-content-filter",
      "engine": "void_loop",
      "kind": "refusal",
      "source": "OpenAI-compatible chat completions `finish_reason: content_filter` (the form Engine B reads)",
      "replies": [
        {
          "json": {
            "choices": [
              {
                "index": 0,
                "message": { "role": "assistant", "content": "" },
                "finish_reason": "content_filter"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
